            <p>
              Administering a tablet to a resistant cat can be challenging. Here are 3 veterinarian-tested methods:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-xs text-slate-700 list-disc list-inside mt-3">
              <li><strong>The Wet Food Crush Method:</strong> Crush the tablet into a fine powder using a spoon. Blend it into a single tablespoon of strong-scented wet food, such as <em>Nourvet Salmon</em> or <em>Fluffy Wet Gravy</em>. Offer this before giving the regular meal so the cat consumes it hungrily.</li>
              <li><strong>The Burrito Towel Wrap:</strong> Snugly wrap the cat in a thick bath towel with only its head exposed. Gently tilt the head backward until the jaw naturally unlocks, pop the tablet deep onto the base of the tongue, close the mouth, and gently stroke the throat until you see the swallow reflex.</li>
              <li><strong>Protective Grooming Boots:</strong> Slip our silicone cat shoes onto the paws during medical administration to prevent claw scratches. Available in our <a href="/shop" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">Pet Shop Gear section</a>.</li>
            </ul>
